---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { substack } from '../data/site.js';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Now — Jonathan A. Hutton"
  description="What Jonathan A. Hutton is focused on right now — current work, what he's exploring next, and what he's open to."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Now</h1>

      <p class="now-note">
        A <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" rel="noopener">now page</a> — what
        I'm focused on at the moment.
        <!-- TODO(jon): confirm you want the "last updated" line; add a date if so. -->
      </p>

      <p>
        Day to day, I'm a Senior Product Manager at the Washington Health Benefit
        Exchange, leading a team of business systems analysts. It's real work with
        real stakes, and I care about doing it well.
      </p>

      <h2>Exploring next</h2>
      <p>
        I'm starting to look at what comes after: transformation and change-agent
        roles, where causing change is the actual mandate rather than a side effect.
        I'm drawn to mission-driven health tech and to civic and government tech that
        actually ships. Player-coach, senior individual-contributor-plus — I want to
        stay close to the building. I'm not looking for more pure people-management.
      </p>

      <h2>Open to</h2>
      <p>
        Conversations, and a small number of engagements, with people building in
        that space. I'm not blowing up my life — but if you're working on something
        that fits, whether that's a build-with-you project or a role where causing
        change is the actual mandate, I'd like to hear about it.
      </p>

      <h2>Also building</h2>
      <p>
        On the side, I'm helping grow the Cloudbase Foundation — a nonprofit
        <!-- TODO(jon): add a one-line description of Cloudbase Foundation's mission, or a link, if you want one. -->
        — and I keep writing: a
        <a href={substack.url} rel="noopener">Substack</a> and a
        second book in progress.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p { font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: var(--space-12); }
  .now-note {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-base) !important;
  }
</style>
